{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f89f40a90ec9d243","name":"card_event_supply_chain","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Base/events/card_event_supply_chain","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SUPPLY CHAIN","text":"Draw a card. If SUPPLY CHAIN is discarded, add 2 copies to your hand with a cost of 1.","flavorText":"Many historians think that the supply chain built and managed by the Allies during WWII was the most advanced of its time and a major contributor to the Allied victory. Their supply chain management helped them move military supplies and armaments across the Pacific Ocean at strategic times. As an example, during the invasion of Normandy on June 6, 1944, the Allies constructed two artificial harbors on Omaha Beach and Gold Beach known as Mulberry A and B. Mulberry A was destroyed by a severe storm 10 days after its construction, however, Mulberry B accommodated over 2.5 million troops, 500,000 vehicles and 4 million tonnes of supplies until its decommissioning in April 1945.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_supply_chain","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_supply_chain_title","SourceString":"SUPPLY CHAIN","LocalizedString":"SUPPLY CHAIN"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_supply_chain_text","SourceString":"Draw a card. If SUPPLY CHAIN is discarded, add 2 copies to your hand with a cost of 1.","LocalizedString":"Draw a card. If SUPPLY CHAIN is discarded, add 2 copies to your hand with a cost of 1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_supply_chain_history","SourceString":"Many historians think that the supply chain built and managed by the Allies during WWII was the most advanced of its time and a major contributor to the Allied victory. Their supply chain management helped them move military supplies and armaments across the Pacific Ocean at strategic times. As an example, during the invasion of Normandy on June 6, 1944, the Allies constructed two artificial harbors on Omaha Beach and Gold Beach known as Mulberry A and B. Mulberry A was destroyed by a severe storm 10 days after its construction, however, Mulberry B accommodated over 2.5 million troops, 500,000 vehicles and 4 million tonnes of supplies until its decommissioning in April 1945.","LocalizedString":"Many historians think that the supply chain built and managed by the Allies during WWII was the most advanced of its time and a major contributor to the Allied victory. Their supply chain management helped them move military supplies and armaments across the Pacific Ocean at strategic times. As an example, during the invasion of Normandy on June 6, 1944, the Allies constructed two artificial harbors on Omaha Beach and Gold Beach known as Mulberry A and B. Mulberry A was destroyed by a severe storm 10 days after its construction, however, Mulberry B accommodated over 2.5 million troops, 500,000 vehicles and 4 million tonnes of supplies until its decommissioning in April 1945."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Motorized_INfantry_Move_FX'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Motorized_INfantry_Move_FX.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_winter_truck.t_winter_truck","SubPathString":""},"artist":"INTERFOTO / Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/SUPPLY_CHAIN.SUPPLY_CHAIN","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":513.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Imperial War Museum","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"LC-USW33-000888-C DLC","historyPhotoAuthor":"Harrison (Sgt), No 5 Army Film & Photographic Unit","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_supply_chain_photo","SourceString":"The Mulberry arti